{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"callout","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Looking for traditional search engine optimization? See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./seo","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SEO guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-is-geo","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What is GEO?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generative Engine Optimization (GEO)"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is the practice of structuring your content and data so that AI systems—like ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, and other LLM-powered tools—can accurately understand, cite, and recommend your content."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"While traditional SEO focuses on ranking in search engine results pages, GEO focuses on being accurately represented in AI-generated responses. As more users get information through AI assistants rather than traditional search, this is becoming increasingly important."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"how-geo-differs-from-seo","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How GEO Differs from SEO"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Aspect"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SEO"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"GEO"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Goal"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rank in search results"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Be cited/recommended by AI"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Audience"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Search engine crawlers"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"LLM training & retrieval systems"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Key signals"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Links, keywords, page speed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structured data, clarity, authority"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Content format"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optimized for snippets"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optimized for extraction & synthesis"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The good news: many GEO best practices overlap with SEO. Clear structure, authoritative content, and good metadata help both."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-tanstack-start-provides","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What TanStack Start Provides"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start's features that support GEO:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server-Side Rendering"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Ensures AI crawlers see fully rendered content"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structured Data"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - JSON-LD support for machine-readable content"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Document Head Management"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Meta tags that AI systems can parse"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Routes"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Create machine-readable endpoints (APIs, feeds)"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"structured-data-for-ai","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structured Data for AI"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structured data using schema.org vocabulary helps AI systems understand your content's meaning and context. This is perhaps the most important GEO technique."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"article-schema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Article Schema"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/posts/$postId.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    const post = await fetchPost(params.postId)\n    return { post }\n  },\n  head: ({ loaderData }) => ({\n    meta: [{ title: loaderData.post.title }],\n    scripts: [\n      {\n        type: 'application/ld+json',\n        children: JSON.stringify({\n          '@context': 'https://schema.org',\n          '@type': 'Article',\n          headline: loaderData.post.title,\n          description: loaderData.post.excerpt,\n          image: loaderData.post.coverImage,\n          author: {\n            '@type': 'Person',\n            name: loaderData.post.author.name,\n            url: loaderData.post.author.url,\n          },\n          publisher: {\n            '@type': 'Organization',\n            name: 'My Company',\n            logo: {\n              '@type': 'ImageObject',\n              url: 'https://myapp.com/logo.png',\n            },\n          },\n          datePublished: loaderData.post.publishedAt,\n          dateModified: loaderData.post.updatedAt,\n        }),\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: PostPage,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"product-schema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Product Schema"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For e-commerce, product schema helps AI assistants provide accurate product information:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/products/$productId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    const product = await fetchProduct(params.productId)\n    return { product }\n  },\n  head: ({ loaderData }) => ({\n    meta: [{ title: loaderData.product.name }],\n    scripts: [\n      {\n        type: 'application/ld+json',\n        children: JSON.stringify({\n          '@context': 'https://schema.org',\n          '@type': 'Product',\n          name: loaderData.product.name,\n          description: loaderData.product.description,\n          image: loaderData.product.images,\n          brand: {\n            '@type': 'Brand',\n            name: loaderData.product.brand,\n          },\n          offers: {\n            '@type': 'Offer',\n            price: loaderData.product.price,\n            priceCurrency: 'USD',\n            availability: loaderData.product.inStock\n              ? 'https://schema.org/InStock'\n              : 'https://schema.org/OutOfStock',\n          },\n          aggregateRating: loaderData.product.rating\n            ? {\n                '@type': 'AggregateRating',\n                ratingValue: loaderData.product.rating,\n                reviewCount: loaderData.product.reviewCount,\n              }\n            : undefined,\n        }),\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: ProductPage,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"organization-and-website-schema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Organization and Website Schema"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add organization schema to your root route for site-wide context:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/__root.tsx\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  head: () => ({\n    meta: [\n      { charSet: 'utf-8' },\n      { name: 'viewport', content: 'width=device-width, initial-scale=1' },\n    ],\n    scripts: [\n      {\n        type: 'application/ld+json',\n        children: JSON.stringify({\n          '@context': 'https://schema.org',\n          '@type': 'WebSite',\n          name: 'My App',\n          url: 'https://myapp.com',\n          publisher: {\n            '@type': 'Organization',\n            name: 'My Company',\n            url: 'https://myapp.com',\n            logo: 'https://myapp.com/logo.png',\n            sameAs: [\n              'https://twitter.com/mycompany',\n              'https://github.com/mycompany',\n            ],\n          },\n        }),\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: RootComponent,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"faq-schema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"FAQ Schema"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"FAQ schema is particularly effective for GEO—AI systems often extract Q&A pairs:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/faq')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const faqs = await fetchFAQs()\n    return { faqs }\n  },\n  head: ({ loaderData }) => ({\n    meta: [{ title: 'Frequently Asked Questions' }],\n    scripts: [\n      {\n        type: 'application/ld+json',\n        children: JSON.stringify({\n          '@context': 'https://schema.org',\n          '@type': 'FAQPage',\n          mainEntity: loaderData.faqs.map((faq) => ({\n            '@type': 'Question',\n            name: faq.question,\n            acceptedAnswer: {\n              '@type': 'Answer',\n              text: faq.answer,\n            },\n          })),\n        }),\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: FAQPage,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"machine-readable-endpoints","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Machine-Readable Endpoints"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create API endpoints that AI systems and developers can consume directly:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/api/products.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/products')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      GET: async ({ request }) => {\n        const url = new URL(request.url)\n        const category = url.searchParams.get('category')\n\n        const products = await fetchProducts({ category })\n\n        return Response.json({\n          '@context': 'https://schema.org',\n          '@type': 'ItemList',\n          itemListElement: products.map((product, index) => ({\n            '@type': 'ListItem',\n            position: index + 1,\n            item: {\n              '@type': 'Product',\n              name: product.name,\n              description: product.description,\n              url: `https://myapp.com/products/${product.id}`,\n            },\n          })),\n        })\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"content-best-practices","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Content Best Practices"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Beyond technical implementation, content structure matters for GEO:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"clear-factual-statements","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clear, Factual Statements"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AI systems extract factual claims. Make your key information explicit:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Good: Clear, extractable facts\nfunction ProductDetails({ product }) {\n  return (\n    <article>\n      <h1>{product.name}</h1>\n      <p>\n        {product.name} is a {product.category} made by {product.brand}. It costs\n        ${product.price} and is available in {product.colors.join(', ')}.\n      </p>\n    </article>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hierarchical-structure","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hierarchical Structure"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use proper heading hierarchy—AI systems use this to understand content organization:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function DocumentationPage() {\n  return (\n    <article>\n      <h1>Getting Started with TanStack Start</h1>\n\n      <section>\n        <h2>Installation</h2>\n        <p>Install TanStack Start using npm...</p>\n\n        <h3>Prerequisites</h3>\n        <p>You'll need Node.js 18 or later...</p>\n      </section>\n\n      <section>\n        <h2>Configuration</h2>\n        <p>Configure your app in your build tool config...</p>\n      </section>\n    </article>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"authoritative-attribution","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Authoritative Attribution"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Include author information and sources—AI systems consider authority signals:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  head: ({ loaderData }) => ({\n    meta: [\n      { title: loaderData.post.title },\n      { name: 'author', content: loaderData.post.author.name },\n      {\n        property: 'article:author',\n        content: loaderData.post.author.profileUrl,\n      },\n      {\n        property: 'article:published_time',\n        content: loaderData.post.publishedAt,\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: PostPage,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"llms-txt","children":[{"type":"text","value":"llms.txt"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some sites are adopting a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"llms.txt"},{"type":"text","value":" file (similar to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"robots.txt"},{"type":"text","value":") to provide guidance to AI systems:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/llms[.]txt.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/llms.txt')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      GET: async () => {\n        const content = `# My App\n\n> My App is a platform for building modern web applications.\n\n## Documentation\n- Getting Started: https://myapp.com/docs/getting-started\n- API Reference: https://myapp.com/docs/api\n\n## Key Facts\n- Built with TanStack Start\n- Supports React and Solid\n- Full TypeScript support\n\n## Contact\n- Website: https://myapp.com\n- GitHub: https://github.com/mycompany/myapp\n`\n\n        return new Response(content, {\n          headers: {\n            'Content-Type': 'text/plain',\n          },\n        })\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"monitoring-ai-citations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Monitoring AI Citations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unlike traditional SEO with established analytics, GEO monitoring is still evolving. Consider:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Test with AI assistants"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Ask ChatGPT, Claude, and Perplexity about your product/content"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Monitor brand mentions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Track how AI systems describe your offerings"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validate structured data"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Use "},{"type":"link","href":"https://search.google.com/test/rich-results","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Google's Rich Results Test"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"https://validator.schema.org/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Schema.org Validator"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check AI search engines"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Monitor presence in Perplexity, Bing Chat, and Google AI Overviews"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"what-is-geo","text":"What is GEO?","level":2},{"id":"how-geo-differs-from-seo","text":"How GEO Differs from SEO","level":2},{"id":"what-tanstack-start-provides","text":"What TanStack Start Provides","level":2},{"id":"structured-data-for-ai","text":"Structured Data for AI","level":2},{"id":"article-schema","text":"Article Schema","level":3},{"id":"product-schema","text":"Product Schema","level":3},{"id":"organization-and-website-schema","text":"Organization and Website Schema","level":3},{"id":"faq-schema","text":"FAQ Schema","level":3},{"id":"machine-readable-endpoints","text":"Machine-Readable Endpoints","level":2},{"id":"content-best-practices","text":"Content Best Practices","level":2},{"id":"clear-factual-statements","text":"Clear, Factual Statements","level":3},{"id":"hierarchical-structure","text":"Hierarchical Structure","level":3},{"id":"authoritative-attribution","text":"Authoritative Attribution","level":3},{"id":"llms-txt","text":"llms.txt","level":2},{"id":"monitoring-ai-citations","text":"Monitoring AI Citations","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n> [!NOTE]\n> Looking for traditional search engine optimization? See the [SEO guide](./seo).\n\n## What is GEO?\n\n**Generative Engine Optimization (GEO)** is the practice of structuring your content and data so that AI systems—like ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, and other LLM-powered tools—can accurately understand, cite, and recommend your content.\n\nWhile traditional SEO focuses on ranking in search engine results pages, GEO focuses on being accurately represented in AI-generated responses. As more users get information through AI assistants rather than traditional search, this is becoming increasingly important.\n\n## How GEO Differs from SEO\n\n| Aspect             | SEO                         | GEO                                  |\n| ------------------ | --------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| **Goal**           | Rank in search results      | Be cited/recommended by AI           |\n| **Audience**       | Search engine crawlers      | LLM training & retrieval systems     |\n| **Key signals**    | Links, keywords, page speed | Structured data, clarity, authority  |\n| **Content format** | Optimized for snippets      | Optimized for extraction & synthesis |\n\nThe good news: many GEO best practices overlap with SEO. Clear structure, authoritative content, and good metadata help both.\n\n## What TanStack Start Provides\n\nTanStack Start's features that support GEO:\n\n- **Server-Side Rendering** - Ensures AI crawlers see fully rendered content\n- **Structured Data** - JSON-LD support for machine-readable content\n- **Document Head Management** - Meta tags that AI systems can parse\n- **Server Routes** - Create machine-readable endpoints (APIs, feeds)\n\n## Structured Data for AI\n\nStructured data using schema.org vocabulary helps AI systems understand your content's meaning and context. This is perhaps the most important GEO technique.\n\n### Article Schema\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/posts/$postId.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    const post = await fetchPost(params.postId)\n    return { post }\n  },\n  head: ({ loaderData }) => ({\n    meta: [{ title: loaderData.post.title }],\n    scripts: [\n      {\n        type: 'application/ld+json',\n        children: JSON.stringify({\n          '@context': 'https://schema.org',\n          '@type': 'Article',\n          headline: loaderData.post.title,\n          description: loaderData.post.excerpt,\n          image: loaderData.post.coverImage,\n          author: {\n            '@type': 'Person',\n            name: loaderData.post.author.name,\n            url: loaderData.post.author.url,\n          },\n          publisher: {\n            '@type': 'Organization',\n            name: 'My Company',\n            logo: {\n              '@type': 'ImageObject',\n              url: 'https://myapp.com/logo.png',\n            },\n          },\n          datePublished: loaderData.post.publishedAt,\n          dateModified: loaderData.post.updatedAt,\n        }),\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: PostPage,\n})\n```\n\n### Product Schema\n\nFor e-commerce, product schema helps AI assistants provide accurate product information:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/products/$productId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    const product = await fetchProduct(params.productId)\n    return { product }\n  },\n  head: ({ loaderData }) => ({\n    meta: [{ title: loaderData.product.name }],\n    scripts: [\n      {\n        type: 'application/ld+json',\n        children: JSON.stringify({\n          '@context': 'https://schema.org',\n          '@type': 'Product',\n          name: loaderData.product.name,\n          description: loaderData.product.description,\n          image: loaderData.product.images,\n          brand: {\n            '@type': 'Brand',\n            name: loaderData.product.brand,\n          },\n          offers: {\n            '@type': 'Offer',\n            price: loaderData.product.price,\n            priceCurrency: 'USD',\n            availability: loaderData.product.inStock\n              ? 'https://schema.org/InStock'\n              : 'https://schema.org/OutOfStock',\n          },\n          aggregateRating: loaderData.product.rating\n            ? {\n                '@type': 'AggregateRating',\n                ratingValue: loaderData.product.rating,\n                reviewCount: loaderData.product.reviewCount,\n              }\n            : undefined,\n        }),\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: ProductPage,\n})\n```\n\n### Organization and Website Schema\n\nAdd organization schema to your root route for site-wide context:\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/__root.tsx\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  head: () => ({\n    meta: [\n      { charSet: 'utf-8' },\n      { name: 'viewport', content: 'width=device-width, initial-scale=1' },\n    ],\n    scripts: [\n      {\n        type: 'application/ld+json',\n        children: JSON.stringify({\n          '@context': 'https://schema.org',\n          '@type': 'WebSite',\n          name: 'My App',\n          url: 'https://myapp.com',\n          publisher: {\n            '@type': 'Organization',\n            name: 'My Company',\n            url: 'https://myapp.com',\n            logo: 'https://myapp.com/logo.png',\n            sameAs: [\n              'https://twitter.com/mycompany',\n              'https://github.com/mycompany',\n            ],\n          },\n        }),\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: RootComponent,\n})\n```\n\n### FAQ Schema\n\nFAQ schema is particularly effective for GEO—AI systems often extract Q&A pairs:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/faq')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    const faqs = await fetchFAQs()\n    return { faqs }\n  },\n  head: ({ loaderData }) => ({\n    meta: [{ title: 'Frequently Asked Questions' }],\n    scripts: [\n      {\n        type: 'application/ld+json',\n        children: JSON.stringify({\n          '@context': 'https://schema.org',\n          '@type': 'FAQPage',\n          mainEntity: loaderData.faqs.map((faq) => ({\n            '@type': 'Question',\n            name: faq.question,\n            acceptedAnswer: {\n              '@type': 'Answer',\n              text: faq.answer,\n            },\n          })),\n        }),\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: FAQPage,\n})\n```\n\n## Machine-Readable Endpoints\n\nCreate API endpoints that AI systems and developers can consume directly:\n\n```ts\n// src/routes/api/products.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/products')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      GET: async ({ request }) => {\n        const url = new URL(request.url)\n        const category = url.searchParams.get('category')\n\n        const products = await fetchProducts({ category })\n\n        return Response.json({\n          '@context': 'https://schema.org',\n          '@type': 'ItemList',\n          itemListElement: products.map((product, index) => ({\n            '@type': 'ListItem',\n            position: index + 1,\n            item: {\n              '@type': 'Product',\n              name: product.name,\n              description: product.description,\n              url: `https://myapp.com/products/${product.id}`,\n            },\n          })),\n        })\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Content Best Practices\n\nBeyond technical implementation, content structure matters for GEO:\n\n### Clear, Factual Statements\n\nAI systems extract factual claims. Make your key information explicit:\n\n```tsx\n// Good: Clear, extractable facts\nfunction ProductDetails({ product }) {\n  return (\n    <article>\n      <h1>{product.name}</h1>\n      <p>\n        {product.name} is a {product.category} made by {product.brand}. It costs\n        ${product.price} and is available in {product.colors.join(', ')}.\n      </p>\n    </article>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Hierarchical Structure\n\nUse proper heading hierarchy—AI systems use this to understand content organization:\n\n```tsx\nfunction DocumentationPage() {\n  return (\n    <article>\n      <h1>Getting Started with TanStack Start</h1>\n\n      <section>\n        <h2>Installation</h2>\n        <p>Install TanStack Start using npm...</p>\n\n        <h3>Prerequisites</h3>\n        <p>You'll need Node.js 18 or later...</p>\n      </section>\n\n      <section>\n        <h2>Configuration</h2>\n        <p>Configure your app in your build tool config...</p>\n      </section>\n    </article>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Authoritative Attribution\n\nInclude author information and sources—AI systems consider authority signals:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  head: ({ loaderData }) => ({\n    meta: [\n      { title: loaderData.post.title },\n      { name: 'author', content: loaderData.post.author.name },\n      {\n        property: 'article:author',\n        content: loaderData.post.author.profileUrl,\n      },\n      {\n        property: 'article:published_time',\n        content: loaderData.post.publishedAt,\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: PostPage,\n})\n```\n\n## llms.txt\n\nSome sites are adopting a `llms.txt` file (similar to `robots.txt`) to provide guidance to AI systems:\n\n```ts\n// src/routes/llms[.]txt.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/llms.txt')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      GET: async () => {\n        const content = `# My App\n\n> My App is a platform for building modern web applications.\n\n## Documentation\n- Getting Started: https://myapp.com/docs/getting-started\n- API Reference: https://myapp.com/docs/api\n\n## Key Facts\n- Built with TanStack Start\n- Supports React and Solid\n- Full TypeScript support\n\n## Contact\n- Website: https://myapp.com\n- GitHub: https://github.com/mycompany/myapp\n`\n\n        return new Response(content, {\n          headers: {\n            'Content-Type': 'text/plain',\n          },\n        })\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Monitoring AI Citations\n\nUnlike traditional SEO with established analytics, GEO monitoring is still evolving. Consider:\n\n- **Test with AI assistants** - Ask ChatGPT, Claude, and Perplexity about your product/content\n- **Monitor brand mentions** - Track how AI systems describe your offerings\n- **Validate structured data** - Use [Google's Rich Results Test](https://search.google.com/test/rich-results) and [Schema.org Validator](https://validator.schema.org/)\n- **Check AI search engines** - Monitor presence in Perplexity, Bing Chat, and Google AI Overviews\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nref: docs/start/framework/react/guide/geo.md\nredirect_from:\n  - /framework/solid/guide/llmo\nreplace:\n  {\n    '@tanstack/react-router': '@tanstack/solid-router',\n    '/framework/react/': '/framework/solid/',\n  }\n---\n"}
